+---
+id: task-003-fix-coupon-give-back-on-cancel-verify-free-shipping-at-50-euros
+type: task
+title: "Fix coupon give-back on cancel, verify free shipping at 50 euros"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+Two reports.
+
+1. Paolo, welcome code refused after cancelling: `OrderService.cancel` called `coupons.giveBack(code,
+   order.customer)`, but `Coupons` records the using order's id, so the coupon was never released. It now
+   passes the order id. Red first: new test in `test/coupons.test.ts` (cancel, then reuse the code).
+2. Support, €4.90 shipping on exactly €50.00 of goods: not reproducible. `shippingCost` already uses `>=`
+   (task-001); the deployed build was probably older. Characterization test added in `test/orders.test.ts`
+   (5 mugs = €50.00 ships free); it passed on its first run, no code change.
